<title>USA: Hawke sees U.S. bank bill passing Senate today.</title>
<headline>Hawke sees U.S. bank bill passing Senate today.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Treasury Undersecretary John Hawke said he expects banking measures, including one to bolster the thrift deposit insurance fund, to pass the Senate Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;It looks like today will be the day it gets through the Senate,&quot; Hawke told reporters before speaking at a banking conference.</p>
<p>The banking measures passed the House Saturday, he said.</p>
</text>
